## Prerequisites

- **JDK {{jvm_target}}+** ([Adoptium](https://adoptium.net/))
- **just** - Command runner ([installation guide](https://github.com/casey/just#installation))
- **codespell** - Spell checker (`brew install codespell`)
- **semgrep** - Static analysis (`brew install semgrep`)
- **trivy** - Dependency vulnerability scanner (`brew install trivy`)

All Kotlin tooling (ktlint, detekt, Kover, Konsist) is provided by Gradle plugins — no separate installation required.

## Setup

Initialize the project environment:

```bash
just init
```

This will:
- Verify prerequisites (java, gradlew, codespell, semgrep, trivy)
- Download and cache all Gradle dependencies

## Usage

Run the main application:

```bash
just run
```

See all available commands:

```bash
just help
```

## Development

### Available Commands

- `just check` - Check prerequisites
- `just init` - Initialize development environment
- `just run` - Run the main application
- `just destroy` - Clean build artifacts
- `just help` - Show available commands

### Code Quality

- `just code-format` - Auto-format code (ktlint)
- `just code-style` - Check code style (ktlint)
- `just code-spell` - Check spelling (codespell)
- `just code-semgrep` - Run custom static analysis (Semgrep)
- `just code-lspchecks` - Run strict compiler checks (allWarningsAsErrors)
- `just code-security` - Run detekt static analysis (bugs, exceptions, complexity)
- `just code-deptry` - Check dependency hygiene (dependency-analysis)
- `just code-architecture` - Run Konsist architecture tests
- `just code-audit` - Scan dependencies for vulnerabilities and outdated versions

### Testing

- `just test` - Run unit tests
- `just test-coverage` - Run tests with coverage ({{coverage_threshold}}% threshold)

### CI

- `just ci` - Run all validation checks (verbose)
- `just ci-quiet` - Run all checks (silent, fail-fast)

The CI pipeline runs the following steps in order:
1. `init` - Initialize environment
2. `code-format` - Auto-format code (ktlint)
3. `code-style` - Check code style (ktlint)
4. `code-spell` - Spell checking
5. `code-semgrep` - Custom static analysis
6. `code-lspchecks` - Strict compiler checks (allWarningsAsErrors)
7. `code-security` - Static analysis (detekt)
8. `code-deptry` - Dependency hygiene
9. `test` - Unit tests
10. `code-architecture` - Architecture tests (Konsist)
11. `test-coverage` - Coverage verification (Kover)
12. `code-audit` - Vulnerability + version scan (trivy + Gradle Versions Plugin)

